# ABSOLUTE OUTPUT CONTRACT (P0)

## A) One command per message-block
- For EACH executed command: output EXACTLY ONE code fence block.
- The block must contain ONLY the raw stdout of that command.

## B) Forbidden inside any ~~~text block
- The command text itself (e.g. `git status --short`).
- Any prompt prefix like `PS C:\...>` or `>` or `cmd.exe` prompt.
- Any extra commentary, labels, or headings.
- Multiple command outputs in one block.

## C) Fail-fast self-check before sending
If any of these appear in the block, STOP and re-run correctly:
- Starts with `PS ` or contains `PS C:\`
- Contains the literal command (e.g. starts with `git `, `powershell `, `cd `)
- Contains `At line:` / parser errors mixed with other command outputs in same block (means multiple runs got merged)
